  `test/unit/platform-window.js` (new), `docs/platform-shim.md`,
  `specs/prd.json`.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - `@electron/remote`'s renderer entry sets `__esModule: true` and
    defines each builtin (`dialog`, `clipboard`, ...) as a lazy
    getter on `exports` via `addBuiltinProperty`, with **no
    `default`**. So `import { dialog } from '@electron/remote'` is
    the correct shape inside the shim -- same situation as
    `material-ui/styles/colors`. The `import remote from
    '@electron/remote'` in `path-selector.js`,
    `subtitles-controller.js` and `torrent-list-controller.js` works
    only because Rolldown's CJS-external interop synthesises a
    default; under Babel (which builds `lib/`) that form would be
    `undefined`. Anything moved into `src/renderer/lib/` must use
    named imports.
  - Stubbing `@electron/remote` in a unit test needs
    `__esModule: true` on the seeded `exports`, otherwise Babel's
    interop wraps the stub in a `default` and the named import reads
    `undefined`. `require.resolve('@electron/remote')` is safe: it
    resolves without executing, so the real module's "cannot be
    required in the browser process" throw never fires.
  - The sync-to-async hazard in `setDimensions` is *ordering*, not
    just plumbing: the `window.screenX`/`outerWidth` reads and the
    maximize check currently describe one instant. US-027 must take
    the DOM reads before the first `await` and collapse the two
    `isMaximized()` calls into one.
