## 2026-07-28 - US-026

Migrate the shell and clipboard call sites to the platform shim.

**What was implemented**

- `components/update-available-modal.js` and
  `components/unsupported-media-modal.js` now
  `import * as shell from '../lib/platform/shell'` and call
  `shell.openExternal(...)` as a promise.
- `components/open-torrent-address-modal.js` imports
  `../lib/platform/clipboard`. `componentDidMount` prefills the field
  from `clipboard.readText().then(...)` instead of synchronously, and
  bails if `this.torrentURL` is gone by the time it resolves.
- `controllers/torrent-list-controller.js` drops `clipboard` from its
  `electron` import and gets a module-level `copyToClipboard(text)`
  helper, which the two "Copy ... Link to Clipboard" context-menu
  items call. Menu `click` handlers cannot await, so the helper is
  where the promise is terminated.
- `main.js` `onPaste` was also on `electron.clipboard.readText()` --
  `docs/platform-shim.md` lists `main.js:497` as a `readText` call
  site, so it is in scope for this story even though the acceptance
  criteria name only the four component/controller files. It now
  imports `./lib/platform/clipboard` and moves `addTorrent(text)` and
  `update()` inside the `.then`, so the re-render still happens after
  the torrent is added.
- Every one of the five promises ends in
  `.catch((err) => dispatch('error', err))` -- the repo's established
  renderer error path -- so nothing floats and nothing is swallowed.
- New `test/unit/platform-boundary.js` walks `src/renderer/**/*.js`
  excluding `lib/platform/` and asserts no file imports `shell` or
  `clipboard` from `electron`, or reads `electron.shell` /
  `electron.clipboard`. Written first: 5 failures before the
  migration, exactly the 5 call sites; 0 after.
- Docblock/`docs/platform-shim.md` status lines updated from "call
  sites are migrated in US-026" to past tense.

**Files changed**

- `src/renderer/components/update-available-modal.js`
- `src/renderer/components/unsupported-media-modal.js`
- `src/renderer/components/open-torrent-address-modal.js`
- `src/renderer/controllers/torrent-list-controller.js`
- `src/renderer/main.js`
- `src/renderer/lib/platform/shell.js`,
  `src/renderer/lib/platform/clipboard.js` (comments only)
- `test/unit/platform-boundary.js` (new)
- `docs/platform-shim.md`, `specs/prd.json`, `progress.log`

**Verification**

- `npm test` passes, 207 assertions, exit 0 (`standard` + `depcheck` +
  `test-unit`).
- `npm run build` exit 0, both halves; `grep -c 'has been
  externalized'` on the Vite stderr is 0.
- Real launch probe (build artifact patched, then rebuilt): wrote a
  magnet URI to the OS clipboard from the main process, dispatched
  `openTorrentAddress`, and read `#torrent-address-field` back --
  `PROBE readText prefill:
  "magnet:?xt=urn:btih:probe00000..."`. That is the migrated
  `clipboard.readText` path running in the real renderer. `init:
  872ms`, both windows up, no new severity-3 console errors (the
  `getCurrentWindow` one is the known pre-existing `electron.remote`
  failure).
- **Not verified empirically:** `shell.openExternal` and
  `clipboard.writeText` at their new call sites. Both are reachable
  only through a native context menu or a modal button that would
  open a real browser window on the user's machine; the shim
  functions themselves have unit tests from US-022. The six-step
  manual smoke test was not run -- this is a non-interactive session.
  The risk sits on the two context-menu copy items and the two
  "open in browser" buttons.

**Learnings for future iterations:**

- **`dispatch('error', err)` is the renderer's error sink** and the
  right tail for every shim promise a migrated call site cannot
  await. `main.js` defines it and `lib/dispatcher` re-exports it;
  components already import `dispatch` alongside `dispatcher`. Use
  `.then(...).catch((err) => dispatch('error', err))` rather than
  making the handler `async`, which would just relocate the floating
  promise into React's callback.
- **A menu `click` handler is a hard await boundary.** Extract a small
  named helper (`copyToClipboard`) instead of inlining `.catch()` in
  the descriptor -- US-029 rewrites these same descriptors and the
  helper survives that rewrite unchanged.
- **`docs/platform-shim.md` lists call sites the acceptance criteria
  omit.** US-026's criteria name four files; the doc's `readText` row
  also names `main.js:497`. Cross-check the doc's tables against the
  criteria at the start of every remaining migration story, or the
  grep criterion in the same story will fail.
- **The boundary grep belongs in a test, not just in the session.**
  `test/unit/platform-boundary.js` reads `src/` (not `build/`, which
  contains no `components/` or `controllers/`) and is the one place a
  migration regression gets caught. Extend its concern list --
  `['shell', 'clipboard']` today -- as each of US-027..US-032 lands,
  until US-034 replaces it with a lint rule.
- **Probing a modal non-interactively:** `wc.executeJavaScript(
  "window.dispatch('openTorrentAddress')")` opens it and the DOM is
  readable ~1.5s later. Seed OS state (clipboard, etc.) from the main
  process with a plain `require('electron')` in the appended probe
  block -- it does not have to come from the renderer.
